.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Richard Slusher and coworkers produced the first experimentally observed squeezed state of light. In terms of the dimensionless field quadratures \hat x = (\hat a+\hat a^\dagger)/\sqrt2 and \hat p = (\hat a-\hat a^\dagger)/(i\sqrt2), a coherent state divides the quantum uncertainty of the electromagnetic field equally between the two conjugate quadratures; a squeezed state redistributes that uncertainty unequally, reducing the noise in one quadrature below the vacuum (shot-noise) variance of 1/2 at the unavoidable cost of increasing it in the other, while the uncertainty product itself remains bounded below. squeezed_state constructs the squeeze-then-displace state">

